WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.457 --> 00:00:04.621
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:04.621 --> 00:00:05.761
Today we're going to talk about

00:00:05.761 --> 00:00:07.898
how you can be a better leader.

00:00:07.898 --> 00:00:09.828
The why clip is my personal favorite,

00:00:09.828 --> 00:00:11.577
and make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.671
for some special bonus clips
as well as my thoughts.

00:00:14.671 --> 00:00:15.718
And as always, if you hear something

00:00:15.718 --> 00:00:16.945
that really resonates with you,

00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:18.667
something that really hit the mark,

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.390
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.411
put quotes around it

00:00:21.411 --> 00:00:24.491
so other people can be
inspired as well, enjoy.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:27.074
(upbeat music)

00:00:41.937 --> 00:00:44.963
- I think building an
organization and building a team.

00:00:44.963 --> 00:00:48.586
The idea that Jack Welch is the hero

00:00:48.586 --> 00:00:51.847
of creating all his value is silly.

00:00:51.847 --> 00:00:54.506
Getting great people in all these jobs,

00:00:54.506 --> 00:00:57.527
it's a team that makes this thing happen.

00:00:57.527 --> 00:01:01.479
And so building a team
is your strongest suit.

00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:03.017
And you got to love your team.

00:01:03.017 --> 00:01:04.966
You got to want your team to be promoted.

00:01:04.966 --> 00:01:07.342
And when you're coming up,

00:01:07.342 --> 00:01:10.842
the biggest problem I find with young MBAs

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.997
at first the job is you shining,

00:01:16.464 --> 00:01:18.979
raising your hand, having the answers.

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:20.246
They want to do that all the time.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.340
They just got out of school,

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.815
they want to show you how smart they are.

00:01:23.815 --> 00:01:27.973
Now the transition to
manager it all changes.

00:01:27.973 --> 00:01:30.496
It's about growing your people, not you.

00:01:30.496 --> 00:01:34.579
You grow from the reflected
glory of your people.

00:01:35.724 --> 00:01:39.010
So it's all about making them flourish.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:42.413
I like to use the line, that
your job is walking around

00:01:42.413 --> 00:01:44.587
with a can of water in one hand,

00:01:44.587 --> 00:01:46.693
a can of fertilizer in the other hand,

00:01:46.693 --> 00:01:50.157
sprinkling on the seeds
and watching them grow.

00:01:50.157 --> 00:01:54.729
You'll get some weeds and you
got to pull those weeds out.

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:56.963
So everyone's not going to flourish,

00:01:56.963 --> 00:02:01.244
but you've got to be
thinking about all the time

00:02:01.244 --> 00:02:04.333
loving to see your people thrive,

00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:07.309
loving to see them get promoted.

00:02:07.309 --> 00:02:08.514
It's a real turn on.

00:02:08.514 --> 00:02:11.066
It is what management is all about.

00:02:11.066 --> 00:02:15.233
It's about bringing to people
great lives, great futures.

00:02:17.762 --> 00:02:20.971
Changing their family's
life, that's a turn on.

00:02:20.971 --> 00:02:25.138
It's a big deal, that's
what you got to think about.

00:02:27.677 --> 00:02:29.940
- My number one belief about leadership is

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.334
you're a servant.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.627
And here what I mean specifically.

00:02:33.627 --> 00:02:37.381
The word hero, that is in the archetype

00:02:37.381 --> 00:02:39.776
of men and you and I, I bet.

00:02:39.776 --> 00:02:41.394
Is it true that inside of you,

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.919
you want you to be the best,
you want to create the best,

00:02:43.919 --> 00:02:45.243
share the best, do the best,

00:02:45.243 --> 00:02:47.239
is that a metaphor for you in your life?

00:02:47.239 --> 00:02:48.072
- Absolutely.

00:02:48.072 --> 00:02:48.905
- Yeah, me too.

00:02:48.905 --> 00:02:50.096
So I think people in this room

00:02:50.096 --> 00:02:51.546
tend to have that as their metaphor.

00:02:51.546 --> 00:02:54.284
So all of us at some level, man
or woman wants to be a hero.

00:02:54.284 --> 00:02:56.817
The word "hero", in it's
Latin root means servo.

00:02:56.817 --> 00:02:58.749
Servo means servant.

00:02:58.749 --> 00:03:00.749
It actually means slave.

00:03:01.854 --> 00:03:04.310
The hero, why they're the hero

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.148
is become the ultimate servant

00:03:06.148 --> 00:03:08.648
of something larger than themself.

00:03:08.648 --> 00:03:10.020
People and so forth.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.325
The person who thinks
they're going to lead

00:03:11.325 --> 00:03:13.969
by demand or by position can only lead

00:03:13.969 --> 00:03:15.234
for a short period of time.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.947
But the person whose idea is serving

00:03:16.947 --> 00:03:19.632
is my belief is, if you can find a way

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.516
to take any group of people and help them

00:03:22.516 --> 00:03:24.842
to experience their needs at a richer,

00:03:24.842 --> 00:03:26.506
deeper level than anyone else,

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:29.018
then together, you guys
can get anything done.

00:03:29.018 --> 00:03:29.851
Anything.

00:03:29.851 --> 00:03:31.188
Now it may not work the first time,

00:03:31.188 --> 00:03:32.726
but together you can get to that point.

00:03:32.726 --> 00:03:34.931
'Cus needs are ultimately
what we're after.

00:03:34.931 --> 00:03:37.189
We're not after the vehicle
we think we're after.

00:03:37.189 --> 00:03:38.649
You get a billion dollars
and then you get it,

00:03:38.649 --> 00:03:40.592
I got plenty of clients and I'll tell you

00:03:40.592 --> 00:03:43.188
it is not the end game.

00:03:43.188 --> 00:03:45.216
And so then they go after
their second billion.

00:03:45.216 --> 00:03:46.877
Or you think it's getting married

00:03:46.877 --> 00:03:47.790
and you get it and you find out

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.865
it's not the end game.

00:03:49.865 --> 00:03:51.511
There are certain needs
that have to be there.

00:03:51.511 --> 00:03:54.485
And the ultimate needs
are growing and giving.

00:03:54.485 --> 00:03:56.607
'Cus you can only feel so
good filled up by yourself.

00:03:56.607 --> 00:03:58.752
So my core belief is, I got to serve.

00:03:58.752 --> 00:04:00.082
If I serve I can lead.

00:04:00.082 --> 00:04:02.628
Because I believe motive does matter.

00:04:02.628 --> 00:04:07.084
If my motive is just to get
you to do something for me,

00:04:07.084 --> 00:04:08.475
there's a certain amount of power

00:04:08.475 --> 00:04:09.713
that I can get to do that.

00:04:09.713 --> 00:04:11.975
If I strategize, if I think, if I feel,

00:04:11.975 --> 00:04:13.835
and also if it serves a greater good.

00:04:13.835 --> 00:04:16.005
Even if I don't intend it.

00:04:16.005 --> 00:04:19.504
If the bumblebee goes to try
to get the nectar it wants,

00:04:19.504 --> 00:04:21.811
it's selfish goal,

00:04:21.811 --> 00:04:24.908
I believe there's a higher
power that guides it all.

00:04:24.908 --> 00:04:26.967
And when that bumblebee goes

00:04:26.967 --> 00:04:28.377
it doesn't intend to give anything,

00:04:28.377 --> 00:04:31.085
but pollen sticks to its legs.

00:04:31.085 --> 00:04:33.541
As it goes about trying
to get what it wants

00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:35.863
that's how flowers are created.

00:04:35.863 --> 00:04:40.330
I really believe that everything
has a web of connection.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:43.570
If your intent is to serve yourself,

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.359
you're still going to serve
something more than yourself

00:04:45.359 --> 00:04:47.211
and you're going to get a
certain amount of insight.

00:04:47.211 --> 00:04:48.849
If your intent and your motive

00:04:48.849 --> 00:04:50.132
is to serve something yourself,

00:04:50.132 --> 00:04:53.688
but also something more, just your kids,

00:04:53.688 --> 00:04:57.101
then I believe you get a
different level of insight.

00:04:57.101 --> 00:05:00.792
And because it's serving
more of what serves life.

00:05:00.792 --> 00:05:04.147
It's not just me, it's me and my family.

00:05:04.147 --> 00:05:06.342
If you're trying to serve a community

00:05:06.342 --> 00:05:08.582
I believe you get a
different level of insight.

00:05:08.582 --> 00:05:09.650
Trying to serve humanity

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:10.648
you get a different level of insight.

00:05:10.648 --> 00:05:11.481
I get emotional thinking about it

00:05:11.481 --> 00:05:14.127
'cus this is why I do what I do.

00:05:14.127 --> 00:05:15.403
So when someone stands up

00:05:15.403 --> 00:05:18.158
it's not about business,
it's not about anything,

00:05:18.158 --> 00:05:19.258
but about serving them.

00:05:19.258 --> 00:05:22.444
So I will use abrasive
or creative language

00:05:22.444 --> 00:05:23.650
I'll use whatever it takes.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.004
Humor, stupidity, I'll make
fun of myself, I'll challenge,

00:05:26.004 --> 00:05:27.943
I'll do anything to serve
that's why I'm here.

00:05:27.943 --> 00:05:29.344
I don't need to do this anymore,

00:05:29.344 --> 00:05:32.856
but I love to see someone
free, alive, and lit up.

00:05:32.856 --> 00:05:34.667
So when that's your motive,

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.538
no matter how people perceive you outside

00:05:36.538 --> 00:05:38.529
if they're around you long enough

00:05:38.529 --> 00:05:40.970
you can't hide what your real motive is.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:42.585
And they'll see it and they'll feel it.

00:05:42.585 --> 00:05:43.691
Motive does matter.

00:05:43.691 --> 00:05:44.783
If it's to serve something higher

00:05:44.783 --> 00:05:46.473
that doesn't mean you
don't get served too.

00:05:46.473 --> 00:05:48.128
And in business you got to be served or

00:05:48.128 --> 00:05:50.067
I used to do business and I'd
lose money in the business

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:52.358
and everybody else was happy.

00:05:52.358 --> 00:05:54.699
And it was wonderful
except I had no business.

00:05:54.699 --> 00:05:57.647
So it's killing the goose
that lays the golden eggs.

00:05:57.647 --> 00:06:00.114
So I've learned to put that balance in,

00:06:00.114 --> 00:06:01.925
but that gives me power.

00:06:01.925 --> 00:06:03.343
That's why time disappears for me.

00:06:03.343 --> 00:06:06.255
'Cus I'm not about
getting some action done,

00:06:06.255 --> 00:06:07.958
I'm about the outcome.

00:06:07.958 --> 00:06:10.182
- My first job out of
college I had a boss who

00:06:10.182 --> 00:06:12.366
believed it was appropriate to

00:06:12.366 --> 00:06:15.685
berate people to get the most of them.

00:06:15.685 --> 00:06:17.127
And I remember, this is a true story,

00:06:17.127 --> 00:06:18.555
I actually sat down with her,

00:06:18.555 --> 00:06:22.207
we used to have these
monthly career updates.

00:06:22.207 --> 00:06:26.501
And she literally said to
me, "You have no talent."

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:28.084
And I went, "None?"

00:06:29.072 --> 00:06:30.822
And she said, "None."

00:06:32.582 --> 00:06:36.405
And the good news was I
thought that was funny.

00:06:36.405 --> 00:06:37.819
'Cus you can't have none.

00:06:37.819 --> 00:06:39.368
Like if you told me I
could only do one thing

00:06:39.368 --> 00:06:40.808
that actually probably
would have hurt more,

00:06:40.808 --> 00:06:41.808
but nothing.

00:06:44.073 --> 00:06:46.953
And so I really paid attention
as to how she managed

00:06:46.953 --> 00:06:51.148
and the rest of my career
did the complete opposite.

00:06:51.148 --> 00:06:52.570
- Give me an example.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:54.393
- I think pointing out people's strengths

00:06:54.393 --> 00:06:57.660
is a lot better than telling
them they have no talent.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:00.115
Also she had this belief
that if you don't look

00:07:00.115 --> 00:07:04.115
harried and insane then
you're not working hard.

00:07:05.136 --> 00:07:08.409
So I remember pretending
that I was stressed out.

00:07:08.409 --> 00:07:09.465
'Cus if I sauntered down the hallway

00:07:09.465 --> 00:07:12.420
and said hi to people she
thought I was doing nothing.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:14.225
So I started pretending, I'd be like,

00:07:14.225 --> 00:07:15.638
"(sighs) I can't talk, I can't talk,"

00:07:15.638 --> 00:07:17.135
and that way she thought I was very busy

00:07:17.135 --> 00:07:19.229
and she left me alone.

00:07:19.229 --> 00:07:21.782
Yeah, honestly in management, you know.

00:07:21.782 --> 00:07:22.815
Treating people with respect,

00:07:22.815 --> 00:07:25.663
being honest about what
they can and can't do,

00:07:25.663 --> 00:07:27.387
and committing yourself to helping people,

00:07:27.387 --> 00:07:30.377
not hurting people and pushing them down

00:07:30.377 --> 00:07:32.591
has been more effective for me.

00:07:32.591 --> 00:07:36.566
- Sometimes at work it's
not what's happening at work

00:07:36.566 --> 00:07:39.583
for a lot of stressed
out managers especially,

00:07:39.583 --> 00:07:41.198
it's what's happening outside of work.

00:07:41.198 --> 00:07:44.421
How do you try to figure
out where the source is

00:07:44.421 --> 00:07:47.545
of the issue maybe to cut
past some of the challenges

00:07:47.545 --> 00:07:48.785
you face communicating?

00:07:48.785 --> 00:07:51.636
- When I was entry-level,
having empathy for my boss

00:07:51.636 --> 00:07:53.053
didn't factor in.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:56.895
Not knowing anything
about sort of my place

00:07:56.895 --> 00:07:58.809
in the company and et cetera.

00:07:58.809 --> 00:08:01.522
But as I've grown up I realized

00:08:01.522 --> 00:08:05.614
that the only motivation for
any kind of confrontation

00:08:05.614 --> 00:08:07.488
whether you're the one
who's confronting someone

00:08:07.488 --> 00:08:10.963
because you feel that they
have done something wrong

00:08:10.963 --> 00:08:12.122
or whether you're confronting them

00:08:12.122 --> 00:08:15.245
because you feel that you've been wronged

00:08:15.245 --> 00:08:18.021
the only motivation is empathy.

00:08:18.021 --> 00:08:20.965
And so even if someone is
coming down on me hard,

00:08:20.965 --> 00:08:24.720
or being unreasonable, or being you know.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.207
I'm not perfect at it,

00:08:26.207 --> 00:08:28.563
but I've worked really hard to approach it

00:08:28.563 --> 00:08:33.231
with confronting them that
they hurt me or I feel wronged,

00:08:33.231 --> 00:08:36.887
but immediately go into
considering that maybe there's

00:08:36.887 --> 00:08:38.703
something that's bothering them.

00:08:38.703 --> 00:08:41.379
And that has proved to be really helpful.

00:08:41.379 --> 00:08:42.879
And we do it in life.

00:08:42.879 --> 00:08:46.957
I mean for example,
somebody sitting next to you

00:08:46.957 --> 00:08:49.938
on the subway is slouched
back they're legs open

00:08:49.938 --> 00:08:54.156
and your immediate reaction
is to think, "What an ass,"

00:08:54.156 --> 00:08:56.006
but the idea of practicing and say,

00:08:56.006 --> 00:08:58.919
"Well maybe he had a hard day yesterday

00:08:58.919 --> 00:09:01.999
and he's exhausted and he
just doesn't want to deal."

00:09:01.999 --> 00:09:05.785
Maybe he doesn't want to talk to people.

00:09:05.785 --> 00:09:08.571
To really just have empathy
for the world around you.

00:09:08.571 --> 00:09:10.531
It's kind of powerful,

00:09:10.531 --> 00:09:12.241
and people respond to
you a lot better as well

00:09:12.241 --> 00:09:15.470
because basically everybody
wants to feel safe.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:17.948
And so if you have empathy
you give that to people

00:09:17.948 --> 00:09:19.756
up or down the chain of command.

00:09:19.756 --> 00:09:22.717
I mean we as employees want to feel safe.

00:09:22.717 --> 00:09:25.543
It is our bosses
responsibility to give us that,

00:09:25.543 --> 00:09:28.585
but at the same time
bosses want to feel safe.

00:09:28.585 --> 00:09:31.847
They don't want to feel
that there's insurrection

00:09:31.847 --> 00:09:33.097
that's brewing.

00:09:34.552 --> 00:09:36.056
And for us to let them know

00:09:36.056 --> 00:09:37.077
that we've got their back

00:09:37.077 --> 00:09:38.644
as much as we want them to let us know

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:40.949
that they have ours is
equally as important.

00:09:40.949 --> 00:09:44.632
And I believe there is
responsibility of a manager,

00:09:44.632 --> 00:09:47.250
but there's a responsibility
of an employee as well.

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.692
It's like the kids have
to do chores at home.

00:09:49.692 --> 00:09:50.939
That's the kind of same thing.

00:09:50.939 --> 00:09:53.055
It's like we all, it takes all of us.

00:09:53.055 --> 00:09:56.279
The hierarchy doesn't mean
that only the guys above

00:09:56.279 --> 00:09:57.521
are the ones with responsibility.

00:09:57.521 --> 00:09:59.209
We all have to contribute.

00:09:59.209 --> 00:10:02.248
- One of the keys to Apple is

00:10:02.248 --> 00:10:06.749
Apple is an incredibly
collaborative company.

00:10:06.749 --> 00:10:07.582
And so...

00:10:10.697 --> 00:10:12.554
You know how many
committees we have at Apple?

00:10:12.554 --> 00:10:13.693
- [Interviewer] No.

00:10:13.693 --> 00:10:15.348
- Zero.

00:10:15.348 --> 00:10:16.587
We have no committees.

00:10:16.587 --> 00:10:17.486
- [Interviewer] No committees.

00:10:17.486 --> 00:10:20.403
- We are organized like a start-up.

00:10:21.834 --> 00:10:25.726
One person is in charge
of iPhone OS software.

00:10:25.726 --> 00:10:28.477
One person is in charge of Mac hardware.

00:10:28.477 --> 00:10:31.580
One person is in charge of
iPhone hardware engineering.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:35.018
Another person is in charge
of world wide marketing.

00:10:35.018 --> 00:10:38.329
Another person is in charge of operations.

00:10:38.329 --> 00:10:40.268
We're organized like a start-up.

00:10:40.268 --> 00:10:43.276
We're the biggest start-up on the planet.

00:10:43.276 --> 00:10:44.526
And we all meet

00:10:46.074 --> 00:10:48.379
for three hours once a week

00:10:48.379 --> 00:10:50.764
and we talk about everything we're doing.

00:10:50.764 --> 00:10:52.166
The whole business.

00:10:52.166 --> 00:10:55.930
And there's tremendous team
work at the top of the company

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:58.594
which filters down to tremendous team work

00:10:58.594 --> 00:11:00.045
throughout the company.

00:11:00.045 --> 00:11:04.051
And team work is dependent
on trusting the other folks

00:11:04.051 --> 00:11:05.767
to come through with their part

00:11:05.767 --> 00:11:07.849
without watching them all the time,

00:11:07.849 --> 00:11:09.646
but trusting that they're
going to come through

00:11:09.646 --> 00:11:10.754
with their parts.

00:11:10.754 --> 00:11:13.991
And that's what we do really well.

00:11:13.991 --> 00:11:15.758
And we're great at figuring out

00:11:15.758 --> 00:11:19.578
how to divide things up into
these great teams that we have

00:11:19.578 --> 00:11:23.716
and all work on the same
thing, touch bases frequently,

00:11:23.716 --> 00:11:26.195
and bring it all together into a product.

00:11:26.195 --> 00:11:27.814
We do that really well.

00:11:27.814 --> 00:11:31.981
And so what I do all day is
meet with teams of people.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:36.543
And work on ideas and solve problems,

00:11:37.715 --> 00:11:40.572
to make new products, to
make new marketing programs,

00:11:40.572 --> 00:11:41.560
whatever it is.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:44.165
- And are people willing
to tell you you're wrong?

00:11:44.165 --> 00:11:46.234
- (laughs) Yeah.

00:11:46.234 --> 00:11:48.512
- [Interviewer] I mean other
than snarky journalists

00:11:48.512 --> 00:11:49.592
I mean people that work for you.

00:11:49.592 --> 00:11:53.684
- Oh yeah, no we have wonderful arguments.

00:11:53.684 --> 00:11:54.973
- [Interviewer] And do
you win them all or?

00:11:54.973 --> 00:11:57.041
- Oh no, I wish I did.

00:11:57.041 --> 00:11:58.668
Well see, you can't.

00:11:58.668 --> 00:12:00.575
If you want to hire great people

00:12:00.575 --> 00:12:02.872
and have them stay working for you

00:12:02.872 --> 00:12:06.181
you have to let them
make a lot of decisions

00:12:06.181 --> 00:12:10.014
and you have to be won
by ideas not hierarchy.

00:12:11.603 --> 00:12:14.150
The best ideas have to win.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:16.482
Otherwise good people don't stay.

00:12:16.482 --> 00:12:18.628
- When you begin leading a new business

00:12:18.628 --> 00:12:20.882
or take on a new leadership
role in a business

00:12:20.882 --> 00:12:23.514
you'd usually be relatively inexperienced

00:12:23.514 --> 00:12:26.387
in the constant thrust
of business activities.

00:12:26.387 --> 00:12:27.915
Because of your lack of experience

00:12:27.915 --> 00:12:30.367
you will go into business
with the wrong people

00:12:30.367 --> 00:12:32.477
and hire the wrong people and get involved

00:12:32.477 --> 00:12:35.145
with the wrong people at many levels.

00:12:35.145 --> 00:12:36.946
Now this is normal and natural

00:12:36.946 --> 00:12:40.044
and it's to be expected at the beginning.

00:12:40.044 --> 00:12:44.691
The key is to always be growing
as a person and as a leader.

00:12:44.691 --> 00:12:46.817
As you continue to grow and learn

00:12:46.817 --> 00:12:49.189
it will reflect on all parts of your life

00:12:49.189 --> 00:12:51.830
and in all parts of your business.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:54.421
There's a universal principle
that you've heard of

00:12:54.421 --> 00:12:56.435
called the Law of Attraction.

00:12:56.435 --> 00:12:59.387
This law says that you
always attract into your life

00:12:59.387 --> 00:13:02.607
the people, and ideas,
and resources, and harmony

00:13:02.607 --> 00:13:05.417
with your dominant thoughts.

00:13:05.417 --> 00:13:08.468
The fact is that you are a living magnet.

00:13:08.468 --> 00:13:11.377
Like iron filings are
attracted to a magnet

00:13:11.377 --> 00:13:13.663
you'll attract into your life the people

00:13:13.663 --> 00:13:16.319
who are in harmony with your current level

00:13:16.319 --> 00:13:19.643
of knowledge and wisdom and experience.

00:13:19.643 --> 00:13:21.143
The good news is that as your

00:13:21.143 --> 00:13:23.593
leadership skills grow and mature,

00:13:23.593 --> 00:13:26.998
you'll attract into your life
better and better people.

00:13:26.998 --> 00:13:30.336
You'll attract better
employees, and better customers,

00:13:30.336 --> 00:13:32.602
and better suppliers, and better bankers,

00:13:32.602 --> 00:13:34.569
and better associates.

00:13:34.569 --> 00:13:37.569
But you'll always get the
people that you deserve

00:13:37.569 --> 00:13:39.353
based on your current level of

00:13:39.353 --> 00:13:42.147
personal and professional development.

00:13:42.147 --> 00:13:44.006
The more you learn and grow,

00:13:44.006 --> 00:13:46.861
the more experiences you
have that you benefit from

00:13:46.861 --> 00:13:49.819
and the wiser you become
as a business person

00:13:49.819 --> 00:13:51.804
the faster and more consistently

00:13:51.804 --> 00:13:54.334
your business will grow as well.

00:13:54.334 --> 00:13:56.503
You'll always attract the type of people

00:13:56.503 --> 00:13:59.254
who are in harmony with your own level

00:13:59.254 --> 00:14:01.119
of personal development.

00:14:01.119 --> 00:14:05.272
The rule is your life only
gets better on the outside

00:14:05.272 --> 00:14:08.105
when you get better on the inside.

00:14:09.044 --> 00:14:11.145
Now your people only get better

00:14:11.145 --> 00:14:13.340
when you become a better manager.

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:14.910
Your customers only get better

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:17.044
when you become a better sales person.

00:14:17.044 --> 00:14:18.356
Your business only gets better

00:14:18.356 --> 00:14:20.956
when you become a better business person.

00:14:20.956 --> 00:14:24.525
There are no shortcuts
and there's no other way.

00:14:24.525 --> 00:14:26.326
Fortunately you are in complete control

00:14:26.326 --> 00:14:28.610
of every aspect of your life.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:30.273
So always be improving yourself

00:14:30.273 --> 00:14:33.364
and you'll start to improve
every other aspect of your life

00:14:33.364 --> 00:14:37.265
around you including your
leadership abilities.

00:14:37.265 --> 00:14:39.466
Continue to improve your leadership skills

00:14:39.466 --> 00:14:42.495
and qualities by practicing these things.

00:14:42.495 --> 00:14:45.002
Read in your field on a regular basis.

00:14:45.002 --> 00:14:47.791
Always be reading about the best practices

00:14:47.791 --> 00:14:50.156
and leadership skills that you can use

00:14:50.156 --> 00:14:52.505
in your personal development as a leader.

00:14:52.505 --> 00:14:54.672
And try them out everyday.

00:14:55.563 --> 00:14:57.041
Listen to audio programs on

00:14:57.041 --> 00:14:59.111
business and leadership success.

00:14:59.111 --> 00:15:01.810
And try out what you
learn in those programs.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:03.497
Attend business seminars.

00:15:03.497 --> 00:15:05.987
This is one of the greatest
learning tools in history.

00:15:05.987 --> 00:15:08.525
You can gain new perspectives and ideas

00:15:08.525 --> 00:15:09.574
relating to your field

00:15:09.574 --> 00:15:12.949
and then put these ideas into action.

00:15:12.949 --> 00:15:15.878
Share ideas in your
business mastermind groups

00:15:15.878 --> 00:15:18.570
and gain ideas from other people.

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:21.458
If something is working well
for someone else in your field

00:15:21.458 --> 00:15:24.421
there's a good chance it
will work for you as well.

00:15:24.421 --> 00:15:29.155
Use other people's great
ideas to improve on yourself.

00:15:29.155 --> 00:15:30.975
As you improve on the inside,

00:15:30.975 --> 00:15:32.995
your business and every part of you life

00:15:32.995 --> 00:15:35.250
will improve on the outside.

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:38.443
The only limits on what you
can accomplish in your business

00:15:38.443 --> 00:15:42.790
are those limits you set on
yourself with your own thinking.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:45.303
You can go as fast and far as you want

00:15:45.303 --> 00:15:49.188
on your way to wealth,
it's completely up to you.

00:15:49.188 --> 00:15:50.938
- A boss's entire job

00:15:52.438 --> 00:15:56.582
is to get the combined
intellect of his team

00:15:56.582 --> 00:16:00.199
to be raised to a new level
and to instill spirit.

00:16:00.199 --> 00:16:03.252
Find everyway to celebrate.

00:16:03.252 --> 00:16:05.909
Find every excuse to have a party.

00:16:05.909 --> 00:16:08.242
Every little victory counts.

00:16:10.298 --> 00:16:13.131
It is so, if a boss can't energize

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:17.261
if he or she can't excite

00:16:17.261 --> 00:16:19.342
and make people want to be there

00:16:19.342 --> 00:16:21.330
they shouldn't have that title.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.347
- So if we think about my
philosophy on leadership

00:16:23.347 --> 00:16:25.311
I believe that it's a leader's job

00:16:25.311 --> 00:16:28.550
to identify the limiting beliefs

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.405
that hold the people on their team back.

00:16:31.405 --> 00:16:33.165
I think you need to help
the people on your team

00:16:33.165 --> 00:16:34.608
believe in themselves more,

00:16:34.608 --> 00:16:36.019
and help them expose these things

00:16:36.019 --> 00:16:37.379
that have been holding them back,

00:16:37.379 --> 00:16:39.245
and give them the path to break through,

00:16:39.245 --> 00:16:41.312
and give them the confidence, and courage,

00:16:41.312 --> 00:16:42.604
and abilities to break through.

00:16:42.604 --> 00:16:44.553
I think it's important that when you are

00:16:44.553 --> 00:16:47.653
challenging somebody to
push, and grow, and learn,

00:16:47.653 --> 00:16:49.045
and get better that it's all done

00:16:49.045 --> 00:16:52.329
with their self interest
in mind not yours.

00:16:52.329 --> 00:16:53.692
And often those will be aligned.

00:16:53.692 --> 00:16:56.056
Somebody's self interest to
be a better sales person,

00:16:56.056 --> 00:16:59.202
a better programmer, a
better graphic designer.

00:16:59.202 --> 00:17:00.701
If that's one of their ambitions,

00:17:00.701 --> 00:17:02.529
that's great for you too being the leader.

00:17:02.529 --> 00:17:05.318
Sometimes it means that you
push them away from the company.

00:17:05.318 --> 00:17:07.233
It means that they have to
go off and do something else

00:17:07.233 --> 00:17:09.175
'cus their dream is to be a baker

00:17:09.175 --> 00:17:11.095
and you don't have an
opportunity for baking

00:17:11.095 --> 00:17:11.928
in your company.

00:17:11.928 --> 00:17:15.474
So don't stick with me and
be a C or D player here

00:17:15.474 --> 00:17:17.018
go be an A player over there.

00:17:17.018 --> 00:17:20.111
People will only do something
for you for so long.

00:17:20.111 --> 00:17:22.137
If you are forcing
someone into do something,

00:17:22.137 --> 00:17:23.668
forcing them to show up on time,

00:17:23.668 --> 00:17:25.279
forcing someone to hit this deadline,

00:17:25.279 --> 00:17:26.573
forcing someone to grow,

00:17:26.573 --> 00:17:27.557
they will do it for a while

00:17:27.557 --> 00:17:29.133
'cus you're paying the bills.

00:17:29.133 --> 00:17:30.703
Because maybe they respect you,

00:17:30.703 --> 00:17:32.546
because maybe they want to make you happy,

00:17:32.546 --> 00:17:34.702
but when people will really give you

00:17:34.702 --> 00:17:35.729
everything they've got is

00:17:35.729 --> 00:17:37.982
because they see how it benefits them.

00:17:37.982 --> 00:17:40.495
It's because it's in their
best interest to do it

00:17:40.495 --> 00:17:42.701
and it's not a sales job,

00:17:42.701 --> 00:17:44.347
it's not trying to convince them

00:17:44.347 --> 00:17:46.861
that doing this action is
going to be good for them.

00:17:46.861 --> 00:17:48.898
It's truly coming from a place of

00:17:48.898 --> 00:17:52.204
I want you to get better for yourself.

00:17:52.204 --> 00:17:54.311
Whether that means you stay
with our company or not

00:17:54.311 --> 00:17:56.170
if you are going to be around us

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.438
you are going to get better.

00:17:57.438 --> 00:17:59.042
We are going to help you break through

00:17:59.042 --> 00:18:00.388
these limiting personal beliefs,

00:18:00.388 --> 00:18:01.990
these actions that are holding you back.

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:05.090
And I think a good leader
brings that with them.

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:08.634
They bring a desire to make
everything around them better.

00:18:08.634 --> 00:18:09.618
The people around them better,

00:18:09.618 --> 00:18:10.848
the environment around them better,

00:18:10.848 --> 00:18:12.247
the customers around them better

00:18:12.247 --> 00:18:15.471
because it's in their best
interest and not yours.

00:18:15.471 --> 00:18:17.223
And they happen to line
up a lot of the times

00:18:17.223 --> 00:18:19.973
which helps you in your business.

00:18:21.454 --> 00:18:22.585
So that's my quick take.

00:18:22.585 --> 00:18:24.772
I'd love to know what do
you think about leadership?

00:18:24.772 --> 00:18:26.579
What are some of the
skills that you've learned

00:18:26.579 --> 00:18:28.690
some of the tricks,
tactics that you've learned

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:30.469
that helped you become a better leader?

00:18:30.469 --> 00:18:32.823
Or some of the things that
you are trying to learn,

00:18:32.823 --> 00:18:34.262
please leave in the comments below.

00:18:34.262 --> 00:18:35.627
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:18:35.627 --> 00:18:37.962
Also what was your favorite
clip in this video?

00:18:37.962 --> 00:18:39.132
What did you learn the most from

00:18:39.132 --> 00:18:41.647
some of the people who
shared some thoughts today.

00:18:41.647 --> 00:18:43.834
Leave in the comments again
I'll join the discussion.

00:18:43.834 --> 00:18:45.559
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:18:45.559 --> 00:18:47.736
I made this video because
abhishek asked me to.

00:18:47.736 --> 00:18:49.147
So if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:18:49.147 --> 00:18:50.828
in the next edition of Believe Life

00:18:50.828 --> 00:18:52.764
leave it in the comments below

00:18:52.764 --> 00:18:53.645
and I'll see what I can do.

00:18:53.645 --> 00:18:55.328
Finally I wanted to give
a quick shout out to

00:18:55.328 --> 00:18:58.200
local Toronto entrepreneur Frank Hoffmann.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.673
Frank thank you so much for picking up

00:18:59.673 --> 00:19:00.628
a copy of my book.

00:19:00.628 --> 00:19:02.916
Thank you for tweeting
that awesome picture out.

00:19:02.916 --> 00:19:04.338
I know there's a lot of other

00:19:04.338 --> 00:19:05.711
people's books in that picture,

00:19:05.711 --> 00:19:08.007
but Your One Word is on the top

00:19:08.007 --> 00:19:10.073
and so I really appreciate that Frank.

00:19:10.073 --> 00:19:10.906
I hope you enjoy the book.

00:19:10.906 --> 00:19:12.689
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:19:12.689 --> 00:19:15.742
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:19:15.742 --> 00:19:19.438
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:19:19.438 --> 00:19:20.938
I'll see you soon.

00:19:26.818 --> 00:19:29.357
- So there's a wonderful
story about listening.

00:19:29.357 --> 00:19:30.321
There's the problem when people say

00:19:30.321 --> 00:19:31.254
you need to be a better listener

00:19:31.254 --> 00:19:32.992
is we are human beings and
we need to communicate.

00:19:32.992 --> 00:19:35.428
And communication is two
ways listening and speaking.

00:19:35.428 --> 00:19:38.086
So everybody's like you got
to be a better listener.

00:19:38.086 --> 00:19:39.698
But here's the best
understanding I have of it.

00:19:39.698 --> 00:19:43.153
So Nelson Mandela is universally
regarded as a great leader.

00:19:43.153 --> 00:19:45.047
Which is important
because different people

00:19:45.047 --> 00:19:46.927
are viewed differently
in different nations,

00:19:46.927 --> 00:19:50.203
but Nelson Mandela universally
regarded as a great leader.

00:19:50.203 --> 00:19:52.559
He was actually the son of a tribal chief.

00:19:52.559 --> 00:19:54.707
And he was asked in an interview once,

00:19:54.707 --> 00:19:56.985
"How did you learn to be a great leader?"

00:19:56.985 --> 00:19:58.349
And he tells the story of how he would go

00:19:58.349 --> 00:19:59.776
to tribal meetings with his father

00:19:59.776 --> 00:20:01.372
and he remembers two things.

00:20:01.372 --> 00:20:03.018
They always sat in a circle

00:20:03.018 --> 00:20:05.726
and his father was
always the last to speak.

00:20:05.726 --> 00:20:08.811
And in terms of leadership and listening,

00:20:08.811 --> 00:20:10.906
I think the idea of be a better listener

00:20:10.906 --> 00:20:12.347
is actually half the advice.

00:20:12.347 --> 00:20:15.165
I think the advice is practice
being the last to speak.

00:20:15.165 --> 00:20:16.630
You see this all the time in meetings

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:17.696
where everybody will sit around a room

00:20:17.696 --> 00:20:19.140
the senior guy will be like,
"Alright here's the problem,

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:19.973
"here's what I think we should do,

00:20:19.973 --> 00:20:21.726
"but I'm really interested
in what your thoughts are

00:20:21.726 --> 00:20:22.559
"so let's go around the room."

00:20:22.559 --> 00:20:23.392
It's too late.

00:20:23.392 --> 00:20:25.061
You've influenced the room.
- You created the footprint.

00:20:25.061 --> 00:20:27.607
- And people bend and
mold as opposed to saying,

00:20:27.607 --> 00:20:30.238
"Here's the problem I'm interested
in what you have to say."

00:20:30.238 --> 00:20:32.868
Without saying anything and not even,

00:20:32.868 --> 00:20:35.857
this takes practice,
not even giving a hint

00:20:35.857 --> 00:20:37.679
whether you agree or disagree.

00:20:37.679 --> 00:20:39.703
If anything you ask
questions to learn more.

00:20:39.703 --> 00:20:41.838
You get the benefit of
hearing everybody's opinion,

00:20:41.838 --> 00:20:43.025
everybody gets to feel heard,

00:20:43.025 --> 00:20:45.441
and then you get to render your opinion.

00:20:45.441 --> 00:20:47.389
- Is part of the interviewing process

00:20:47.389 --> 00:20:50.202
do you essentially culture check?

00:20:50.202 --> 00:20:53.169
- Yes, but not like a checklist.

00:20:53.169 --> 00:20:57.209
Culture's always something
that we interview for.

00:20:57.209 --> 00:21:01.376
Of kind of curiosity and it's
easy to find people who say,

00:21:02.308 --> 00:21:03.712
"Oh I read the Netflix culture deck

00:21:03.712 --> 00:21:05.819
"I love it I really want to be there."

00:21:05.819 --> 00:21:08.288
What's harder is what are the main things

00:21:08.288 --> 00:21:10.799
you disagree with and why?

00:21:10.799 --> 00:21:12.967
And when we get a blank stare we're like,

00:21:12.967 --> 00:21:15.682
okay not really a first principle thinker

00:21:15.682 --> 00:21:17.635
and when they say,

00:21:17.635 --> 00:21:21.219
"Well I thought the way
that you didn't talk about

00:21:21.219 --> 00:21:25.357
"how to acculturate and if
I'm not great in day three

00:21:25.357 --> 00:21:27.190
"am I out or is there,

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:31.113
"do you look at it like an athlete

00:21:31.113 --> 00:21:33.791
"where it's over some time
period to prove yourself

00:21:33.791 --> 00:21:35.580
"and if so, what's that time period

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:36.986
"and why haven't you clarified that?"

00:21:36.986 --> 00:21:39.115
Then we're like, "Oh yeah,
that's a good insight."

00:21:39.115 --> 00:21:39.972
First principle thinker.

00:21:39.972 --> 00:21:44.236
So we're looking for
people who are curious,

00:21:44.236 --> 00:21:48.319
typically self confident,
and they're questioning

00:21:49.194 --> 00:21:50.842
everything around them.

00:21:50.842 --> 00:21:53.605
- Another important quality
in an effective leader

00:21:53.605 --> 00:21:55.363
is to be a role model.

00:21:55.363 --> 00:21:57.325
To be the kind of person
that everyone else

00:21:57.325 --> 00:21:59.945
looks up to, wants to be like.

00:21:59.945 --> 00:22:02.683
This is true in your work,
in your personal life,

00:22:02.683 --> 00:22:03.892
it's true in your family,

00:22:03.892 --> 00:22:06.269
but it's also true as a manager.

00:22:06.269 --> 00:22:09.342
Effective leaders carry
themselves at all times

00:22:09.342 --> 00:22:11.885
even when no one is watching,

00:22:11.885 --> 00:22:14.218
as if everyone was watching.

00:22:15.563 --> 00:22:18.855
Leaders imagine that they
live in a gold fish bowl

00:22:18.855 --> 00:22:22.806
and everyone is watching the
leader in the leadership role.

00:22:22.806 --> 00:22:24.776
They're very aware of the impact

00:22:24.776 --> 00:22:28.901
of their words and gestures
on the people around them.

00:22:28.901 --> 00:22:32.598
They realize that what they
say has tremendous impact.

00:22:32.598 --> 00:22:34.581
So you must always be sensitive

00:22:34.581 --> 00:22:37.213
to the fact that everything you say or do

00:22:37.213 --> 00:22:41.380
is magnified many times by
the people who look up to you

00:22:42.293 --> 00:22:44.876
or look up to you for guidance.

00:22:46.014 --> 00:22:48.574
A positive remark from you to someone

00:22:48.574 --> 00:22:51.780
over whom you exert influence or control

00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:54.795
has inordinately positive effects.

00:22:54.795 --> 00:22:57.366
A negative remark or criticism from you

00:22:57.366 --> 00:23:00.338
has inordinately negative effects.

00:23:00.338 --> 00:23:03.573
The impact of both are multiplied.

00:23:03.573 --> 00:23:07.731
So choose your words and
your behavior with care.

00:23:07.731 --> 00:23:11.264
If you aspire to become an
inspirational and effective

00:23:11.264 --> 00:23:13.963
leader you must continuously
work on yourself

00:23:13.963 --> 00:23:16.616
and improve your management skills.

00:23:16.616 --> 00:23:20.339
No one starts off as an
effective leader or manager,

00:23:20.339 --> 00:23:22.772
but you can aspire to improve your skills

00:23:22.772 --> 00:23:25.482
by learning what leaders
do, and how they think,

00:23:25.482 --> 00:23:27.983
and how they feel, and
then by copying them

00:23:27.983 --> 00:23:30.938
until you become one yourself.

00:23:30.938 --> 00:23:33.708
Remember leaders are made not born

00:23:33.708 --> 00:23:37.249
and they are self made
through personal development.

